      "shortDescription": "VACON is a Danfoss Drives brand for variable-speed drives and power-conversion equipment. The current portfolio includes low-voltage, enclosed, decentralised, system and medium-voltage drive platforms, alongside software, options and lifecycle support for active and legacy products.",
      "fullDescription": [
        "VACON originated in Finland in 1994 and became part of the Danfoss Group in December 2014. Danfoss continues to use VACON as a product brand within Danfoss Drives, with engineering and production activity associated with its Vaasa operation.",
        "The active VACON portfolio includes compact and industrial low-voltage drives, pump-and-fan drives, decentralised drives, system modules, enclosed drives and medium-voltage platforms. Published families include VACON 20, VACON 100 INDUSTRIAL, VACON 100 FLOW, VACON 100 X, VACON NXS, VACON NXP and VACON 3000, while Danfoss also maintains documentation and lifecycle services for discontinued VACON ranges. Applications documented by Danfoss include industrial machinery, pumps and fans, HVAC, water treatment, marine and offshore, material handling and energy systems."
