      "shortDescription": "VEM develops and manufactures electric motors, generators and controlled drive systems through its German group companies and production sites. Its portfolio ranges from low-voltage standard and special motors to large high-voltage machines, traction drives, marine equipment and customised power-generation solutions.",
      "fullDescription": [
        "VEM is a German drive-technology group whose official history traces its industrial roots to 1886. The current organisation operates through VEM GmbH, VEM motors GmbH and VEM Sachsenwerk GmbH, with production in Dresden, Wernigerode and Zwickau; official company history records the group's acquisition by SEC Holding Ltd. China in 2017.",
        "The VEM programme covers IEC and special low-voltage motors, medium- and high-voltage asynchronous and synchronous motors, permanent-magnet machines, traction motors, marine drives, wind and hydro generators, and complete controlled-drive systems. Product variants include explosion-protected, brake, roller-table, water-cooled, high-speed, slip-ring and application-specific designs. The group documents applications across pumps, fans, compressors, cranes, rolling mills, mining equipment, marine propulsion, public transport and power generation."
      ],
